\section{Index re-estimation}{
With \code{reestimate_index = TRUE}, the covariance matrices are re-estimated
from each cycle's own simulated data, which is what a breeding programme
actually does and which propagates estimation error across cycles. With
\code{FALSE}, the coefficients from cycle one are reused, which isolates the
effect of the desired-gain direction itself. A large divergence between the
two settings means the recommendation is sensitive to estimation error, and
the breeder should be told so.
